/P 131 0 R
/E (The CMA report is used as a methodological benchmark as it provides a complete, evidence-based assessment of the cloud market under the Enterprise Act. The EU investigation is ongoing and focuses on assessing whether similar market features and practices exist that may limit competitiveness and fairness \(European Commission, 2025\).  )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (The CMA Final Decision Report shows that the CMA gathered evidence by consulting a large number of stakeholders, including UK customers, major cloud providers, independent software vendors \(ISVs\), and academics. The CMA focused primarily on qualitative evidence, expressing concerns that quantitative surveys in this complex market lacked validity. In addition, the CMA conducted rigorous financial assessments, including a profitability analysis comparing Return on Capital Employed \(ROCE\) to Weighted Average Cost of Capital \(WACC\). To investigate the licensing tie, the CMA analysed quantitative pricing data by comparing the effective prices Microsoft charges its own Azure customers for Windows Server and SQL Server against the higher input prices it charges users of rival cloud providers for the same software \(CMA, 2025\). )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
