236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (Each additional enterprise customer, therefore, strengthens the rationale for the next enterprise to choose the same provider. This creates a self-reinforcing ecosystem dynamic that favours incumbents. At the platform level, a second compounding dynamic emerges with two-sided characteristics. Because enterprise customers are already concentrated on the leading hyperscalers, independent software vendors and tool-builders such as Databricks and Snowflake may have strong incentives to build their products around those platforms to access that customer base. This is consistent with a richer ecosystem of integrated tools on leading platforms than on smaller rivals, which in turn attracts more enterprise customers, reinforcing the original advantage. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
