/E (The key harm channel is reduced contestability: when ecosystems reinforce incumbency, rivals must overcome not only price/quality gaps but also coordination advantages embedded in training, integrations and complementary service availability. This contributes to reducing contestability and sustained market concentration, particularly when combined with switching barriers identified in the CMA investigation.  )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
